save(163,dict(paragraphs=["Garima Garg is a poet and translator associated with Panchkula, Haryana. Alongside her Hindi poems, her work includes bringing Pradeep Biswal’s poetry into Punjabi. The Pioneer reported the release of that translation, published by Shalandi Books, at the Toshali Literature Festival in February 2023.","Her two poems in Kabita Live approach language as a means of connection and agency. ‘एहसास’ moves through appeals for humane conversation, care for the earth and relief from sorrow. ‘कलम हथियार लायी हूँ’ gives the pen a sharp edge without losing tenderness: its speaker brings feeling, colour and the fragrance of flowers into the act of writing."],sources=[source('The Pioneer — Odia poet Biswal’s works in Punjabi released, February15 2023','https://www.dailypioneer.com/uploads/2023/epaper/february/bhubaneswar-english-edition-2023-02-15.pdf',['Garima Garg, Panchkula poet; Punjabi translation of Pradeep Biswal; Shalandi Books; Toshali festival release.'])],identity_match='Captured biography names Garima Garg, Panchkula and Hindi/Punjabi/English translation; report independently agrees on locality and Punjabi translation activity. Delhi journalist and other namesakes excluded.',poems_read=[dict(id=144,title='एहसास',basis='Full Hindi original read: humane guidance, conversation, earth care and grief; Garima signature.'),dict(id=271,title='कलम हथियार लायी हूँ',basis='Full Hindi original read: repeated pen-as-weapon refrain, strength, emotional articulation, colours and flowers.')],limitations=['Older writer-profiles works array is empty; authoritative publication JSON links poems144 and271 to writer163, and those were read. No source or membership changed.','Romanized translation title in news report not independently reconciled with book cover; omitted exact title and purchase link.','Reported language abilities not treated as formal qualifications.'],next_action='Independent author/editor review; confirm preferred Punjabi title and book page.'))
